INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<p>Cultivation <strong>Sultana grapes</strong> Due to its fine root structure and requirement for stable soil moisture, it is considered one of the most challenging vegetable crops. Many farmers believe that simply installing drip tape is sufficient, but field experience shows that <strong>regular maintenance</strong> of the system, rather than the installation itself, is the decisive factor for crop quality and economic yield. Drip tape, due to its small emitter spacing (typically 15 to 18 millimeters) and narrow diameter, is susceptible to physical and chemical clogging. If proper maintenance is not performed, you will face root-zone water stress in the middle of the season and experience flower and fruit drop. Below, we examine the comprehensive maintenance pathway for drip tape in Sultana vineyards step by step.</p><h2>Technical inspection of the system before the start of the planting season</h2><p>Before Sultana seed placement, the irrigation system must be tested for full integrity. This stage is the most critical part of maintenance. At this stage, you must measure the input pressure to the tape using a manometer. The desired pressure for standard drip tape is typically between 0.5 and 0.7 bar. Higher pressure causes rupture and irregular distribution, while lower pressure fails to deliver water to root depth.</p><ul><li><strong>Filter inspection:</strong> Screen and sand filters must be cleaned thoroughly. Calcium deposits or sludge in the filter are the first signs of neglecting maintenance.</li><li><strong>Leak test:</strong> All metal and plastic joints must be checked. Even a single drop of leakage per kilometer of line can cause pressure drop at the end of the line.</li><li><strong>Nozzle flow rate adjustment:</strong> Water discharge rate must be uniform. If any nozzles have lower flow rates than the others, they are likely clogged and require repair or replacement.</li></ul><p>It is also recommended to use drip tapes made of high-density polyethylene (HDPE), which offer a longer service life against UV radiation and mechanical stresses from field operations.</p><h2>Addressing drip tape clogging</h2><p>Drip tape clogging occurs in two forms: physical clogging (caused by sediment, algae, and suspended particles) and chemical clogging (caused by changes in water pH or salt precipitation). To prevent physical clogging, a robust filtration system is your primary line of defense. Wire-mesh filters with 100 or 120 mesh are generally suitable for drip tapes, but if your well water has high sediment levels, disc filters should also be used.</p><h3>Irrigation line flushing and restoration methods</h3><p>When you observe signs of clogging (changes in discharge water color, reduced flow rate, or dry soil between rows), take the following actions:</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/نگهداری-شاهی-با-نوار-تیپ-نکات-کلیدی-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="نگهداری شاهی با نوار تیپ: نکات کلیدی - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>crop drip tape maintenance care Shahi</figcaption></figure><ol><li><strong>Back-flush (Reverse Flush):</strong> Open the drip tape outlet and reverse the water flow toward the outlet through a side valve. This removes suspended particles from the tape emitters.</li><li><strong>Acid application:</strong> In cases of calcium scale, injecting citric acid or fluorosilicic acid (at a controlled dose) into the system via a chlorinator or dosing pump will dissolve these deposits. <em>Note:</em> Never pour acid directly into the drip tape; it must be diluted in the main tank and then injected through the system.</li><li><strong>Chlorine flushing:</strong> To eliminate algae and bacteria, using liquid chlorine at a concentration of 1 to 2 mg/L in the tank is highly effective. This process should be repeated monthly.</li></ol><p>A key point in maintaining pomegranate drip tape is not to repair surface cracks with special adhesive; adhesives may block the emitters. It is better to use spare tape pieces made of the same material.</p><div class="image-container"></div><h2>Impact of proper maintenance on pomegranate yield</h2><p>Pomegranate is a crop highly sensitive to drought stress. When drip tape is properly maintained and water distribution is uniform, the fine pomegranate roots at a soil depth of 15 to 20 cm receive sufficient moisture. This allows the plant\'s energy to be directed toward fruit production rather than survival. Estimates indicate that farms with properly flushed, clog-free drip tape systems achieve yields 15 to 20% higher than those with partial clogs.</p><p>If you are seeking overall optimization of your cultivation, familiarizing yourself with other agricultural indicators is useful. For example, in vegetable fields, knowing <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/comprehensive-guide-cucumber-drip-irrigation-tajik/">Comprehensive guide to cucumber drip irrigation</a> It can provide a similar model for other vegetables such as cilantro, as the principles of filter maintenance and pressure for plants with fine root systems are similar. Also, although our focus is on cilantro, understanding the relationship between irrigation and yield in other crops like <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/mung-bean-seed-amount-per-hectare/">Knowing the seed quantity of sesame per hectare</a> helps you utilize the appropriate cropping pattern (even and odd year planting) to reduce water stress in your farms.</p><div class="image-container"></div><h2>Practical maintenance tips for different seasons</h2><p>Drip tape maintenance is a continuous task, not a seasonal event. In hot months, rapid algae growth begins inside and outside the tape. To address this issue, you should adjust irrigation times to early morning or evening so that algae do not multiply under direct sunlight at high temperatures. Additionally, in colder months, high water temperature from the well can cause vapor cycling in the tape and increase clogging; in these cases, using disk filters with easy cleaning capabilities is essential.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/نگهداری-شاهی-با-نوار-تیپ-نکات-کلیدی-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="نگهداری شاهی با نوار تیپ: نکات کلیدی - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>crop drip tape maintenance care cilantro</figcaption></figure><h3>Planning for the end of the season</h3><p>After harvesting the cilantro crop, do not remove the drip tape from the field (if you intend to reuse it for the next season). Place the tape in the shade and avoid exposing it to direct sunlight. The best practice is to flush the tape near the well with low pressure (30-40% of working pressure) for 30 minutes to remove internal sediments. Then fold it and store it in a cool, dark place. This small step extends the useful life of the tape by 2-3 seasons.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Maintenance operations</th><th>Time interval</th><th>Objective</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Filter inspection</td><td>Once a week</td><td>Prevent clogging at nozzles</td></tr><tr><td>Acid or chlorine flush</td><td>Monthly</td><td>Internal cleaning of the tape</td></tr><tr><td>Control of outlet pressure</td><td>Monthly</td><td>Verify irrigation uniformity</td></tr><tr><td>Visual inspection of the tape</td><td>After each irrigation</td><td>Identification of tears or extra holes</td></tr></tbody></table><p>It should be noted that water quality is the backbone of tape maintenance. If you are using old wells with high sediment, you may need pre-filtration systems. Study about <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/licorice-harvest-yield-per-hectare-factors/">Factors affecting stem yield per hectare</a> It demonstrates how minor changes in water quality and irrigation can impact the taste and shelf life of the final crop; although the plant species differ, the logic of maintaining quality through precise micro-irrigation control is shared. Additionally, for farmers cultivating in drier regions, familiarity with <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/asparagus-yield-per-hectare-iraq-guide/">the Asparagus Performance Guide in Iraq</a> can provide a deeper understanding of irrigation challenges in climates similar to certain regions of Iran, where precise drip irrigation management is critical.</p><div class="image-container"></div><h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2><h3>Can drip tape be cleaned with high pressure?</h3><p>No. Pressures exceeding 1 bar can damage the tape wall, causing holes to widen or the tape to rupture. Always perform cleaning at the system\'s working pressure (typically 0.5 to 0.7 bar).</p><h3>What is the best time to clean the filters?</h3><p>Once a week, preferably when the pump is off or operating at low pressure, open and rinse the filters. If there is heavy sediment, use a diluted citric acid solution to clean the filters.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/نگهداری-شاهی-با-نوار-تیپ-نکات-کلیدی-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="نگهداری شاهی با نوار تیپ: نکات کلیدی - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>crop drip tape maintenance care شاهی</figcaption></figure><h3>Why is water not coming out of some drip tape emitters?</h3><p>Possible causes: mechanical clogging (sediment particles), biological clogging (algae), or air entering the tape line (open outlet during pump downtime). First, keep the outlet closed to allow extra air to escape, then perform a flush.</p><h3>Can fertigation be used in شاهی drip tape?</h3><p>Yes, but only with soluble fertilizers. Do not apply nitrate- or ammonia-rich fertilizers directly to the شاهی roots to prevent fine root burn. Always use a dosing pump or an injection tank to ensure the fertilizer is thoroughly mixed into the main tank.</p><h2>Summary and final recommendation</h2><p>Maintaining drip tape in a شاهی crop is an investment whose return can be directly measured in improved root and leaf quality, resulting in increased fruit weight and a higher selling price. Regular monitoring, periodic flushing, and smart water resource management are the keys to your success. Do not forget that your irrigation system is the beating heart of the farm; caring for it is caring for the crop. By following the points outlined in this شاهی drip tape maintenance guide, you can minimize water-stress risk and system clogging. Success in precision agriculture is hidden in the details, and شاهی requires those details.</p>','Saffron Maintenance Using a T-Strip: Key Strategies for Enhanced Productivity','Spinach is a vegetable highly sensitive to root-zone moisture. Drip irrigation can be highly effective, but only if the system is properly maintained. This article covers the key maintenance tips for drip systems in spinach production to help you protect your investment and achieve optimal performance.','publish','closed','closed','saffron-maintenance-t-strip-enhanced-productivity',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
